  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "A high-fat meal leaves peak and total exposure comparable to fasting. It is 95% bound to plasma protein and is mainly eliminated in feces, with about 14% in urine.",
    "substance": "A mesylate salt. The parent compound has a molecular weight of 499.6.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA as 40 mg and 80 mg tablets, taken once daily.",
    "safety": "No boxed warning, and no contraindications are listed. Diarrhea (47%) and rash (46%) are the most common reactions.",
    "indication": "Adjuvant therapy after tumor resection, and treatment of stage III or metastatic non-small cell lung cancer, in patients whose tumors carry specific mutations.",
    "mechanism": "Irreversibly inhibits mutant forms of EGFR (T790M, L858R, exon 19 deletions), binding them at about 9-fold lower concentrations than wild-type."
  },
  "tell": "A roughly 48-hour half-life and about threefold accumulation on once-daily dosing set this EGFR inhibitor apart.",
